@startuml AutomaticSaveSequenceDiagram
' @@author naieel04
' One successful save; filesystem messages summarize operations and the replacement strategy.
participant ":FinNUS" as FinNUS
participant "storage:FileStorage" as Storage
participant "codec:LedgerCodec" as Codec
participant "<<class>>\nFiles" as Files

note over FinNUS
    Ledger changes are pending and saving is allowed.
    Capture the current ledger snapshot.
end note
FinNUS -> Storage: save(snapshot)
activate Storage
note over Storage, Files
    File operations are summarised.
    Preserve damaged files before replacement.
end note
Storage -> Codec: encode(snapshot)
activate Codec
Codec --> Storage: text
deactivate Codec
Storage -> Files: writeString(...)
Files --> Storage: return
opt main file exists and is known clean
    Storage -> Files: save previous ledger as backup
    Files --> Storage: return
end
Storage -> Files: atomically replace main file
Files --> Storage: return
Storage --> FinNUS: return
deactivate Storage
note over FinNUS
    Clear pending changes after saving.
    Failed saves remain pending for retry after
    a successful command or at shutdown.
end note
@enduml
